From: Swift Linux <noreply@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] wpe: export JavaScriptCore's C API and install its headers

WPE WebKit builds JavaScriptCore into libWPEWebKit with its C API (JSBase.h's
JS_EXPORT functions, Apple's API), but its symbol map exports only jsc_*,
webkit_* and wpe_*, and it installs only the GLib API's headers. WebKitGTK's
javascriptcoregtk library exports the C API and installs its headers.

Export JS* and kJS* too, and install the C API's headers under
wpe-webkit-2.0/JavaScriptCore, which wpe-webkit-2.0's pkg-config Cflags put
<JavaScriptCore/JavaScript.h> in reach of. A program written against Apple's
JavaScriptCore C API, such as Perry's JavaScriptCore provider, can then use
WPE WebKit's, on a system with no GTK.
---
--- a/Source/JavaScriptCore/PlatformWPE.cmake
+++ b/Source/JavaScriptCore/PlatformWPE.cmake
@@ -22,3 +22,8 @@
     DESTINATION "${CMAKE_INSTALL_INCLUDEDIR}/wpe-webkit-${WPE_API_VERSION}/jsc"
     COMPONENT "Development"
 )
+
+install(FILES ${JavaScriptCore_PUBLIC_FRAMEWORK_HEADERS}
+    DESTINATION "${CMAKE_INSTALL_INCLUDEDIR}/wpe-webkit-${WPE_API_VERSION}/JavaScriptCore"
+    COMPONENT "Development"
+)
--- a/Source/WebKit/webkitglib-symbols.map
+++ b/Source/WebKit/webkitglib-symbols.map
@@ -1,5 +1,7 @@
 {
 global:
+  JS*;
+  kJS*;
   jsc_*;
   webkit_*;
   wpe_*;
